# COVERAGE FIXTURE. Deliberate test data, not an ontology about anything.
#
# RULE: scm-avf2
# W3C OWL 2 Web Ontology Language Profiles (Second Edition), section 4.3,
# Table 9: The Semantics of Schema Vocabulary.
# https://www.w3.org/TR/owl2-profiles/#Reasoning_in_OWL_2_RL_and_RDF_Graphs_using_Rules
#
#   T(?c1, owl:allValuesFrom, ?y)
#   T(?c1, owl:onProperty, ?p1)
#   T(?c2, owl:allValuesFrom, ?y)
#   T(?c2, owl:onProperty, ?p2)
#   T(?p1, rdfs:subPropertyOf, ?p2)
#     ->  T(?c2, rdfs:subClassOf, ?c1)
#
# WHY IT EXISTS. Same shape as scm-svf2.ttl with allValuesFrom in place of
# someValuesFrom, and nothing in this repository has it, so
# tools/horn_differential.py compared the Rust and Python engines on scm-avf2
# zero times and its clean sweep said nothing about it.
#
# NOTE THE DIRECTION. The consequent is T(?c2, rdfs:subClassOf, ?c1), which is
# the REVERSE of scm-svf2's. Universal quantification is antitone in the
# property: widening the property narrows the class. A transcription that
# copied the someValuesFrom row and changed the vocabulary would get the
# direction wrong, and with no corpus document firing the rule nothing would
# have noticed. This fixture is what would notice, because it pins which of
# :R1 and :R2 is the subclass.
#
# EXPECTED: exactly one derivation, credited to scm-avf2:
#   :R2 rdfs:subClassOf :R1
#
# scm-avf1 does not also fire: it would need :C rdfs:subClassOf :C, which this
# file does not assert, and the built-in table has no reflexivity rule.

@prefix : <http://ex.org/cover/scm-avf2#> .
@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .

:R1 a owl:Restriction ;
    owl:onProperty :p1 ;
    owl:allValuesFrom :C .

:R2 a owl:Restriction ;
    owl:onProperty :p2 ;
    owl:allValuesFrom :C .

:p1 rdfs:subPropertyOf :p2 .
